 $b.$\n\n- The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n- The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now check our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. We have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =det[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =1\\cdot 3-(-1)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =5\\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the fifth part of the invertible matrix theorem is true, all the other parts of the theorem are true too. Therefore, according to the theorem:\n\n- Statement II is true by the second part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement III is false. According to the first part of the invertible matrix theorem, the inverse ${A}^{-1}$ must exist.\n\nFinally, only statements I and II are true." 13194139535088 true] [17592186330500 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330501 13194139535088 true] [17592186330500 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330502 13194139535088 true] [17592186330500 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330503 13194139535088 true] [17592186330500 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330504 13194139535088 true] [17592186330500 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330505 13194139535088 true] [17592186330500 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535088 true] [17592186330500 1041 "selection" 13194139535088 true] [17592186330500 1104 #edb/ref 17592186330504 13194139535088 true] [17592186330500 1110 #uuid "6caa1713-bf48-55c7-9f1d-6bfe6fd74b09" 13194139535088 true] [17592186330501 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535088 true] [17592186330501 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535088 true] [17592186330501 1111 #uuid "99c52999-8c6c-555e-8840-1cd4bab11dc7" 13194139535088 true] [17592186330502 1034 "I only" 13194139535088 true] [17592186330502 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535088 true] [17592186330502 1111 #uuid "9290c049-23b5-50a3-ade1-aaa4a9e2e85f" 13194139535088 true] [17592186330503 1034 "III only" 13194139535088 true] [17592186330503 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535088 tru